'''Carlos Eduardo Gutiérrez Mancilla'''{{Family name footnote|[[Gutiérrez]]|[[Mancilla (surname)|Mancilla]]|lang=Mexican}} (born 19 August 1994) is a Mexican politician from the [[Institutional Revolutionary Party]] (PRI). He is a native of [[Tuxtla Gutiérrez]], Chiapas.<ref name=sil66/>

In the [[2024 Mexican general election|2024 general election]], he was elected to a [[Electoral regions of Mexico|plurinominal seat]] in the [[Chamber of Deputies (Mexico)|Chamber of Deputies]] for the duration of the [[LXVI Legislature of the Mexican Congress|66th Congress]].<ref name=sil66>{{cite web|url=https://sil.gobernacion.gob.mx/Librerias/pp_PerfilLegislador.php?Referencia=9229282|title=Perfil: Dip. Carlos Eduardo Gutiérrez Mancilla, LXVI Legislatura |publisher=[[Secretariat of the Interior|SEGOB]] |website=Sistema de Información Legislativa (SIL)|language=es |accessdate=4 September 2026}}</ref> He is also the president of the [[youth wing]] of the [[COPPPAL|Permanent Conference of Political Parties of Latin America and the Caribbean]] (COPPPAL).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.copppal.org/la-copppal/directoriojuvenil/|title=Directiva de la COPPPAL Juvenil|publisher=[[COPPPAL]]|date=27 November 2024|language=es}}</ref>

Gutiérrez Mancilla has been involved in several instances of [[legislative violence]] during his congressional term.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Viedma |first1=Jaqueline |title=Este es el historial de peleas violentas de Carlos Mancilla, legislador del PRI y cercano a Alito Moreno |url=https://www.infobae.com/mexico/2026/08/12/este-es-el-historial-de-peleas-violentas-de-carlos-mancilla-legislador-del-pri-y-cercano-a-alito-moreno/ |work=[[Infobae]] |date=12 August 2026}}</ref>

