'''Melvin Tchiknavorian''' (born 3 September 1997) is a French [[Freestyle skiing|freestyle skier]] specializing in [[ski cross]]. He represented France at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]].

==Career==
Tchiknavorian made his first international appearance on 19 December 2015 in Val Thorens, where he finished 29th in the FIS competition.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=208830&raceid=9335 | title = Val Thorens (FRA) FIS Men's Ski Cross December 19, 2015 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref> In 2016, he finished 30th at the Junior World Championships in Val Thorens.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=208830&raceid=9339 | title = Val Thorens (FRA) FIS Junior World Ski Championships Men's Ski Cross March 24, 2016 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref>

Tchiknavorian made his first appearance in the World Cup on 11 December 2021 in Val Thorens, where he finished 61st.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=208830&raceid=14440 | title = Val Thorens (FRA) World Cup Men's Ski Cross December 11, 2021 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref> He scored his first points a day later in the same place, finishing 16th.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=208830&raceid=14108 | title = Val Thorens (FRA) World Cup Men's Ski Cross December 12, 2021 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref> He achieved his first podium finish in a World Cup competition on 24 February 2024 in Reiteralm, finishing third. He was only beaten by Sweden's [[Erik Mobärg]] and [[Jonas Lenherr]] from Switzerland.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=208830&raceid=16184 | title = Reiteralm (AUT) World Cup Men's Ski Cross February 24, 2024 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref>

At the [[FIS Freestyle Ski and Snowboarding World Championships 2025|2025 World Championships]] in Engadine, Tchiknavorian won the silver medal in the team competition with [[Jade Grillet-Aubert]].<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=190042&raceid=17163 | title = Engadin (SUI) World Championships Mixed Ski Cross Team March 22, 2025 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.lequipe.fr/Skicross/Actualites/Jade-grillet-aubert-et-melvin-tchiknavorian-arrachent-l-argent-dans-l-epreuve-de-skicross-par-equipes-aux-mondiaux/1548711|title=Jade Grillet-Aubert et Melvin Tchiknavorian arrachent l'argent dans l'épreuve de skicross par équipes aux Mondiaux|author=Dorine Besson|publisher=[[L’Équipe]]|language=fr|date=2025-03-22|access-date=2025-03-23}}</ref> He also finished eighth in the individual competition.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.fis-ski.com/DB/general/results.html?sectorcode=FS&competitorid=190042&raceid=17161 | title = Engadin (SUI) World Championships Men's Ski Cross March 21, 2025 | website = fis-ski.com | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref>

==Personal life==
Tchiknavorian is the younger cousin of [[Terence Tchiknavorian]] who also became a freestyle skier.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.equipedefrance.com/athlete/melvin-tchiknavorian | title = Melvin Tchiknavorian | website = equipedefrance.com | language = fr | access-date = 2026-02-02}}</ref> Both of them are of Armenian descent.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thearmenianreport.com/post/armenian-athletes-competing-for-other-countries-at-the-2026-winter-olympics|title=Armenian Athletes Competing for Other Countries at the 2026 Winter Olympics|website=The Armenian Report|date=5 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://sportaran.com/en/post/armyanskie-sportsmeny-v-sostave-drugih-stran-na-zimnej-olimpiade-2026/|title=Armenian athletes will be competing alongside other countries at the 2026 Winter Olympics: brothers from France and a star from Russia|publisher=Sportran|date=5 February 2026}}</ref>

