'''Yeimi Carina Murcia Yela''' (born {{Circa}} 1990) is a Colombian social communicator and politician who served as [[Ministry of Information and Communications Technology (Colombia)|Minister of Information and Communications Technology]] from 2025 to 2026 under President [[Gustavo Petro]]. 

Born in [[Puerto Asís]], [[Putumayo Department|Putumayo]], she holds a degree in [[social communication]] from the [[Cooperative University of Colombia]].

In 2023 she worked as an advisor to the [[Ministry of Health and Social Protection (Colombia)|Ministry of Health and Social Protection]] under Minister [[Guillermo Alfonso Jaramillo]], later serving as director of ICT appropriation, in 2025 she assumed the position of [[Ministry of Information and Communications Technology (Colombia)|Deputy Minister of Digital Transformation]] and was then appointed and subsequently confirmed by President [[Gustavo Petro]] as [[Ministry of Information and Communications Technology (Colombia)|Minister of Information and Communications Technology]]

==Early life==
Yeimi Carina Murcia Yela was born in {{Circa}} 1990 in [[Puerto Asís]], [[Putumayo Department|Putumayo]]. Her parents fled Puerto Asís for [[Yacopí]], [[Cundinamarca Department|Cundinamarca]], when she was four years old due to the armed conflict.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://elpais.com/america-colombia/2025-09-17/gustavo-petro-rectifica-y-elige-a-carina-murcia-como-ministra-de-las-tic.html|title=Gustavo Petro rectifica y elige a Carina Murcia como ministra de las TIC |trans-title=Gustavo Petro adjusts and chooses Carina Murcia as TIC minister|access-date=March 3, 2026|date=October 15, 2025|last=Triana Sánchez|first=Santiago|work=[[El País]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://elpais.com/america-colombia/2025-09-17/gustavo-petro-rectifica-y-elige-a-carina-murcia-como-ministra-de-las-tic.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.elcolombiano.com/tendencias/como-decidir-entre-una-especializacion-o-maestria-OA18819777|title=¿Cómo decidir entre una especialización o maestría?|trans-title=How to decide between a specialisation or a master's degree?|access-date=March 2, 2026|date=October 10, 2022|work=[[El Colombiano]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.elcolombiano.com/tendencias/como-decidir-entre-una-especializacion-o-maestria-OA18819777|url-status=live}}</ref> She studied [[social communication]] at the [[Cooperative University of Colombia]]. She holds a specialization in government, management, and public affairs from [[Universidad Externado de Colombia]] and more later a master's degree in human rights, democracy and globalisation from the [[Open University of Catalonia]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.eltiempo.com/vida/educacion/educacion-superior-cual-es-la-diferencias-entre-una-maestria-y-una-especializacion-849482|title=Educación superior: ¿Cuál es la diferencias entre una maestría y una especialización?|trans-title=Higher education: What is the difference between a master's degree and a specialisation?|access-date=March 3, 2026|date=January 29, 2024|last=Larrarte Asaad|first=Daniela Viviana|work=[[El Tiempo (Colombia)|El Tiempo]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.eltiempo.com/vida/educacion/educacion-superior-cual-es-la-diferencias-entre-una-maestria-y-una-especializacion-849482|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Political career==
In 2022, she began working at the [[Ministry of Information and Communications Technology (Colombia)|Ministry of Information and Communications Technologies]] as an advisor under Minister [[Sandra Urrutia]]. In 2023, she served as Director of Appropriation, initially under Minister [[Mauricio Lizcano]] and later under Minister [[Julián Molina (politician)|Julián Molina]] after Lizcano's resignation.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.infobae.com/colombia/2025/09/18/quien-es-carina-murcia-la-cuarta-ministra-de-las-tic-en-el-gobierno-petro-seria-cuota-del-partido-de-la-u/|title=Quién es Carina Murcia, la cuarta ministra de las TIC en el Gobierno Petro: sería cuota del Partido de la U|trans-title=Who is Carina Murcia, the fourth ICT minister in the Petro government: would she be a quota appointment from the U Party?|access-date=March 8, 2026|date=September 18, 2025|last=Bernal|first=Jhon|work=[[Infobae]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.infobae.com/colombia/2025/09/18/quien-es-carina-murcia-la-cuarta-ministra-de-las-tic-en-el-gobierno-petro-seria-cuota-del-partido-de-la-u/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In September 2025, she was appointed [[Ministry of Information and Communications Technology (Colombia)|Deputy Minister of Digital Transformation]], and subsequently, on September 21, she assumed the position of Minister of Information and Communications Technologies following Julián Molina's resignation.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.eltiempo.com/politica/gobierno/carina-murcia-viceministra-de-transformacion-digital-queda-a-cargo-de-ministerio-de-las-tic-tras-salida-de-julian-molina-3489220|title=Carina Murcia, viceministra de Transformación Digital, queda a cargo de Ministerio de las TIC tras salida de Julián Molina|trans-title=Carina Murcia, Deputy Minister for Digital Transformation, takes charge of the Ministry of TIC following the departure of Julián Molina|access-date=March 3, 2026|date=October 9, 2025|last=Castillo|first=Camilo A.|work=[[El Tiempo (Colombia)|El Tiempo]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.eltiempo.com/politica/gobierno/carina-murcia-viceministra-de-transformacion-digital-queda-a-cargo-de-ministerio-de-las-tic-tras-salida-de-julian-molina-3489220|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.elcolombiano.com/colombia/mintic-carina-murcia-nombramiento-remplaza-gloria-perdomo-CL29227566|title=Tras una semana, el Gobierno se echó para atrás en nombramiento de Gloria Perdomo como MinTIC y designa a Carina Murcia|trans-title=After a week, the government backed down on Gloria Perdomo's appointment to MinTIC and appointed Carina Murcia instead|access-date=March 4, 2026|date=October 18, 2025|work=[[El Colombiano]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.elcolombiano.com/colombia/mintic-carina-murcia-nombramiento-remplaza-gloria-perdomo-CL29227566|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.eltiempo.com/politica/gobierno/carina-murcia-ya-es-ministra-de-las-tic-fue-posesionada-en-discreta-ceremonia-previo-al-viaje-del-presidente-gustavo-petro-a-nueva-york-3492908|title=Carina Murcia ya es ministra de las TIC|trans-title=Carina Murcia is now Minister of the TIC|access-date=March 3, 2026|date=October 22, 2025|last=García Agudelo|first=Mateo|work=[[El Tiempo (Colombia)|El Tiempo]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.eltiempo.com/politica/gobierno/carina-murcia-ya-es-ministra-de-las-tic-fue-posesionada-en-discreta-ceremonia-previo-al-viaje-del-presidente-gustavo-petro-a-nueva-york-3492908|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.eltiempo.com/tecnosfera/novedades-tecnologia/carina-murcia-ministra-tic-mi-principal-legado-sera-trabajar-por-el-cierre-de-la-brecha-de-genero-en-este-sector-3494951|title=Carina Murcia, ministra TIC: 'Mi principal legado será trabajar por el cierre de la brecha de género en este sector'|trans-title=Carina Murcia, ICT Minister: 'My main legacy will be working to close the gender gap in this sector'|access-date=March 3, 2026|date=October 29, 2025|last=García Rico|first=José Carlos|work=[[El Tiempo (Colombia)|El Tiempo]]|language=Spanish|archive-date=May 6, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506220645/https://www.eltiempo.com/tecnosfera/novedades-tecnologia/carina-murcia-ministra-tic-mi-principal-legado-sera-trabajar-por-el-cierre-de-la-brecha-de-genero-en-este-sector-3494951|url-status=live}}</ref>

