'''Jessica Berenice García Quijano''' (born 23 September 1995) is a [[Mexicans|Mexican]] para-taekwondo athlete.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Vega |first=Patricia |date=July 2024 |title=La reina del parataekwondo |trans-title=The queen of parataekwondo |url=https://www.revistadelauniversidad.mx/articles/9ba6d00e-d55a-4b99-85ec-4169d69ede22/la-reina-del-parataekwondo |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Revistadela Universidad |language=es |quote=Jessica García ... Jessica Berenice García Quijano ... Cuando nació en Mérida, Yucatán, el 23 de septiembre de 1995}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Jessica Garcia Quijano - Taekwondo &#124; Paralympic Athlete Profile |url=https://www.paralympic.org/jessica-garcia-quijano |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=International Paralympic Committee |language=en}}</ref>

== Early life ==
Garcia was born in [[Mérida, Yucatán|Mérida]], Yucatán, on 23 September 1995.<ref name=":0" /> When she was eight, her father put her in a taekwondo school in Mérida, Yucatán.  From 2003 to 2015, she trained with able-bodied opponents to gain experience.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |date=9 November 2023 |title=Jessica García: 20 años para ser reina del parataekwondo |url=https://www.eleconomista.com.mx/deportes/Jessica-Garcia-20-anos-para-ser-reina-del-parataekwondo-20231109-0024.html |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=El Economista |language=es |quote=Jessica Berenice García Quijano}}</ref>

== Career ==
In 2022, she finished second in the world rankings in her category.<ref>{{Cite web |title=TaekwondoData |url=http://www.taekwondodata.com/ |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=TaekwondoData.com |language=en}}</ref>

She won the 52&nbsp;kg category, defeating Egyptian Salma Ali Abd 3–1, in the 2023 World Para-Taekwondo Championships held in Boca del Río, [[Veracruz]].<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.insidethegames.biz/articles/garcia-quijano-home-para-taekwondo-win |title=Inside The Games • Garcia Quijano wins first major title at home World Para Taekwondo Championships |website=Insidethegames.biz |access-date=10 June 2026 |quote=Jessica Garcia Quijano}}</ref> Thus she became the first Mexican woman world champion in this discipline.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Maya |first=La Jornada |date=29 November 2022 |title=Conoce a ganadores del Premio Estatal y el Mérito Deportivo Yucateco 2022 |url=https://www.lajornadamaya.mx/yucatan/207132/conoce-a-ganadores-del-premio-estatal-y-el-merito-deportivo-yucateco-2022 |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Lajornadamaya.mx |language=es |quote=Jessica Berenice García Quijano}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mediotiempo |first=Editorial |date=29 March 2026 |title=Jessica García gana oro histórico en Mundial de Para Taekwondo |url=https://www.mediotiempo.com/mas-deportes/jessica-garcia-gana-oro-historico-en-mundial-de-para-taekwondo-veracruz-2023 |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Mediotiempo |language=es-mx |quote=Jessica Berenice García Quijano}}</ref> She also won a silver, in the K44-52, at the Parapan American games at [[Santiago]], Chile in November 2023.<ref name=":1" />

In 2024, she won a silver medal at the 9th Asian Taekwondo Championships at city of Da Nang, Vietnam,  in the K44 -52&nbsp;kg category after losing in the final to [[Surenjav Ulambayar]] of [[Mongolia]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Quintal |first=Por Johnny Oliver |title=La yucateca Jessica Berenice García Quijano, ganó la presea plateada en Vietnam |url=https://www.jhonnyoliverquintal.com/2024/05/la-yucateca-jessica-berenice-garcia.html |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Johnny Oliver Quintal}}</ref>

Before the [[2020 Summer Paralympics|Tokyo Paralympics]], she moved to [[Mexico City]] to train at the National High Performance Center (CNAR). In her debut at the Paralympics in Paris 2024, she finished fifth.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Deporte |first=Comisión Nacional de Cultura Física y |title=Campeona Jessica García busca revalidar título en Mundial de Para Taekwondo 2025 |url=http://www.gob.mx/conade/articulos/campeona-jessica-garcia-busca-revalidar-titulo-en-mundial-de-para-taekwondo-2025-387439 |access-date=29 March 2026 |website=Gob.mx |language=es |quote=Jessica Berenice García Quijano}}</ref>

